## 3. Integration Pattern Catalog

This section categorizes all in-scope work into three patterns. The pattern selected in Section 2 mechanically determines several downstream decisions.

### Pattern Decision Matrix

| Trigger element | Sync / Async | Layer(s) | Pattern |
|---|---|---|---|
| `http:listener` | Synchronous request/response | sys / proc / exp | **3.1 HTTP Listener API** |
| `anypoint-mq:subscriber` | Async (consumer) | proc | **3.2 Anypoint MQ Consumer** |
| `salesforce-pub-sub:subscribe-channel-listener` | Async (event-driven) | exp API | **3.3 Salesforce Pub/Sub Event App** |

Each pattern is described with the same template (Trigger / Main Flow / Context Variable / Required Global Configs / Outbound Calls / Error Handling / Retry & Idempotency / Health Check / MUnit Mock Surface / Required Env-Property Keys / When to Choose). All snippets are embedded — no external reference projects required.

---

### 3.1 HTTP Listener API (sys / proc / exp)

**Trigger:**

```xml
<http:listener path="${http.basePath}" config-ref="api-listener_config">
    <http:response statusCode="#[vars.httpStatus default 200]">
        <http:headers><![CDATA[#[vars.outboundHeaders default {}]]]></http:headers>
    </http:response>
    <http:error-response statusCode="#[vars.httpStatus default 500]">
        <http:body><![CDATA[#[payload]]]></http:body>
        <http:headers><![CDATA[#[vars.outboundHeaders default {}]]]></http:headers>
    </http:error-response>
</http:listener>
```

**Main flow shape — `{api-spec}-main`:**

```xml
<flow name="{api-spec}-main">
    <http:listener path="${http.basePath}" config-ref="api-listener_config">
        <http:response statusCode="#[vars.httpStatus default 200]">
            <http:headers><![CDATA[#[vars.outboundHeaders default {}]]]></http:headers>
        </http:response>
        <http:error-response statusCode="#[vars.httpStatus default 500]">
            <http:body><![CDATA[#[payload]]]></http:body>
        </http:error-response>
    </http:listener>
    <ee:transform doc:name="Set Request Context">
        <ee:message />
        <ee:variables>
            <ee:set-variable resource="dwls/v-request-context.dwl" variableName="requestContext" />
        </ee:variables>
    </ee:transform>
    <apikit:router config-ref="{api-spec}_config" />
    <error-handler ref="global-error-handler" />
</flow>
```

**Context variable:** `vars.requestContext` — set in the main flow before APIKit router via `dwls/v-request-context.dwl` (see Section 15 for the canonical DWL content).

**Required global configs in `global-config.xml`:**

- `api-listener_config` — `http:listener-config`
- `{api-spec}_config` — `apikit:config`
- `custom-logger-connector_config` — `module-logger:config`
- `azure-key-vault-properties-provider_config` — Azure Key Vault properties provider
- One or more `http-{target}-server_http-request_config` — `http:request-config` per downstream system (only when calling downstream)
- `api-autodiscovery_config` — `api-gateway:autodiscovery`
- `notification-connector_config` — `module-notification:config` (add when notification connector is used; see Section 11 for the required self-closing XML declaration and property keys)

**Outbound calls:** Set `vars.targetApiParams` via DWL, then `flow-ref` to `{downstream-sys-api}-request-flow` (per-system named flow with static `config-ref`). See Section 9.

**Error handling:** Global error handler defined in `global-error-handler.xml` returns a structured error response (`correlationId`, `status`, `code`, `message`) via `on-error-continue`. HTTP status from `errors/customErrors.dwl`. See Section 12.

**Retry / idempotency:** `until-successful` for transient HTTP errors inside each `{downstream-sys-api}-request-flow` (Section 9). Idempotency at the listener is the caller's responsibility unless an `Idempotency-Key` header is contractually defined.

**Health check expectation:** Both `GET /ping` (liveness — no dependency check) and `GET /health-check` (readiness — calls each downstream `/health-check`) are required for HTTP APIs. See Section 10.

**MUnit mock surface:** Mock every `http:request` to downstream systems per endpoint. Set `vars.requestContext` via `munit:variable` when flow-ref'ing directly to API flows (bypassing the main flow).

**Required env-property keys (subset of Section 7):**

- `api.id`, `http.host`, `http.port`, `http.basePath`, `http.timeout`, `http.idleTimeout`
- `request.timeout`, `request.idleTimeout`, `retry.attempts`, `retry.interval`
- `httpErrors`, `timezone`, `sourceSystem`, `targetSystem`
- For each downstream `{system}`: `{system}.host`, `{system}.basePath`, `{system}.client_id`, `{system}.client_secret`; if health-check is exposed, `{system}.healthCheck.method`, `{system}.healthCheck.path`
- `logger.category`, `logger.sensitiveKeyParts`, `logger.safeKeys`, `logger.encryptionKey`

**When to choose:** Synchronous request/response APIs at any layer (sys = direct backend wrapper; proc = orchestration; exp = client-shaped).

**Reference Templates (available in this workspace):**

- **Sys / Exp API (Salesforce CRUD):** `agents/develop/templates/sf-http-sys-api-template/`
  Scaffold keys: `create-record-sub-flow`, `get-records-sub-flow`, `update-record-sub-flow`, `sf-composite-request-sub-flow`; DWLs in `dwls/`; 3 MUnit suites in `src/test/munit/`.
  Use when the Jira story involves Salesforce CRUD via an HTTP-synchronous sys-API or exp-API.

- **Proc API (HTTP orchestration):** `agents/develop/templates/http-proc-api-template/`
  Scaffold keys: `{operation}-sub-flow` with scatter-gather + conditional routes; single dynamic `outbound-sapi-http-request_config`; `async-error-flow-sub-flow`; `post-transactions-errors-sub-flow`; `errors/errorCatalog.dwl`.
  Key differences from sys-API template: single dynamic outbound config (not per-SF-object static configs), async error logging to `sfl-crm-persona-sys-api /transactions-errors`, `errors/errorCatalog.dwl` for per-SAPI transaction IDs, `src/main/resources/application-types.xml`.
  Use when the Jira story is a synchronous HTTP proc API orchestrating multiple downstream SAPIs with optional parallel operations.

