### 3.2 Anypoint MQ Consumer (event-driven proc API)

**Trigger:**

```xml
<anypoint-mq:subscriber doc:name="MQ Subscriber"
    config-ref="anypoint-mq_config"
    destination="${mq.queueName}"
    acknowledgementMode="AUTO">
    <reconnect frequency="${mq.reconnection.frequency}" count="${mq.reconnection.attempts}"/>
    <anypoint-mq:subscriber-type>
        <anypoint-mq:prefetch maxLocalMessages="${mq.maxLocalMessages}" />
    </anypoint-mq:subscriber-type>
    <anypoint-mq:circuit-breaker
        tripTimeout="${mq.subscriber.circuitBreaker.tripTimeout}"
        errorsThreshold="${mq.subscriber.circuitBreaker.errorsThreshold}"/>
</anypoint-mq:subscriber>
```

**Main flow shape — `{queue-name}-mq-consumer`:**

```xml
<flow name="{queue-name}-mq-consumer">
    <anypoint-mq:subscriber doc:name="MQ Subscriber"
        config-ref="anypoint-mq_config"
        destination="${mq.queueName}"
        acknowledgementMode="AUTO">
        <reconnect frequency="${mq.reconnection.frequency}" count="${mq.reconnection.attempts}"/>
        <anypoint-mq:subscriber-type>
            <anypoint-mq:prefetch maxLocalMessages="${mq.maxLocalMessages}" />
        </anypoint-mq:subscriber-type>
        <anypoint-mq:circuit-breaker
            tripTimeout="${mq.subscriber.circuitBreaker.tripTimeout}"
            errorsThreshold="${mq.subscriber.circuitBreaker.errorsThreshold}"/>
    </anypoint-mq:subscriber>
    <tracing:with-correlation-id correlationId="#[attributes.properties.correlationId default correlationId]">
        <module-logger:build-log-with-encrypted-payload doc:name="Received MQ message"
            config-ref="custom-logger-connector_config"
            message="Received message from the MQ"
            sourceSystem="#[attributes.properties.SourceSystem]"
            targetSystem="#[p('targetSystem')]"
            tracepoint="BEFORE_HTTP_REQUEST">
            <module-logger:body><![CDATA[#[output application/json ---
{
    "Payload received": payload,
    "Properties received": attributes.properties
}]]]></module-logger:body>
        </module-logger:build-log-with-encrypted-payload>
        <try>
            <ee:transform doc:name="Request to Downstream">
                <ee:message />
                <ee:variables>
                    <ee:set-variable resource="dwls/v-targetApiParams-{system}.dwl" variableName="targetApiParams" />
                    <ee:set-variable resource="dwls/p-initial-vars.dwl" variableName="initialVar" />
                </ee:variables>
            </ee:transform>
            <flow-ref name="{downstream-sys-api}-request-flow"/>
            <error-handler>
                <on-error-continue doc:name="On Error Continue">
                    <module-logger:build-error-log-with-encrypted-payload
                        config-ref="custom-logger-connector_config"
                        message="Downstream call failed"
                        logLevel="ERROR" tracepoint="EXCEPTION"
                        sourceSystem="#[vars.initialVar.sourceSystem]"
                        targetSystem="#[vars.initialVar.targetSystem]"
                        entityDetails="#[vars.initialVar.entityDetails default null]"
                        cause='#[error.cause.localizedMessage default error.detailedDescription default ""]'
                        errorType='#[(error.errorType.namespace default "UNKNOWN") ++ ":" ++ (error.errorType.identifier default "UNKNOWN")]'
                        errorDescription='#[vars.errorDetails.detailedDescription default error.description default ""]'
                        errorCode="#[vars.errorDetails.cause.errorMessage.attributes.statusCode default 500]">
                        <module-logger:body><![CDATA[#[output application/json ---
{
    "Payload received": vars.initialVar.originalPayload,
    "Properties received": attributes.properties
}]]]></module-logger:body>
                    </module-logger:build-error-log-with-encrypted-payload>
                </on-error-continue>
            </error-handler>
        </try>
        <flow-ref name="success-response-sub-flow"/>
    </tracing:with-correlation-id>
</flow>
```

**Context variable:** `vars.initialVar` — set via `dwls/p-initial-vars.dwl` (see Section 15 for the canonical DWL content).

**Required global configs in `global-config.xml`:**

- `anypoint-mq_config` — Anypoint MQ connector with reconnection
- `custom-logger-connector_config`
- `azure-key-vault-properties-provider_config`
- `notification-connector_config` — `module-notification:config` (recommended; see Section 11 for the required self-closing XML declaration and property keys)
- One or more `http-{target}-server_http-request_config` per downstream system

**Outbound calls:** Same pattern as 3.1 — set `vars.targetApiParams` via DWL, then `flow-ref` to `{downstream-sys-api}-request-flow` (per-system named flow with static `config-ref`). See Section 9.

**Error handling:** Per-message `on-error-continue` to prevent message loss. Failed messages are routed via the global error handler to `publish-to-dlq-sub-flow` (publishes to `${mq.dlq.queueName}` via `anypoint-mq:publish`) and `send-notification-sub-flow` (notification on DLQ publish). See Section 12.

**Retry / idempotency:** `until-successful` for transient downstream HTTP errors. AUTO ack + circuit-breaker + reconnect on the subscriber. **Idempotency:** include a dedupe key in `attributes.properties` and check against an Object Store before processing (recommended for at-least-once delivery semantics).

**Health check expectation:** Optional. The app has no HTTP listener; if a heartbeat is required, expose it via a separate scheduler-driven flow.

**MUnit mock surface:** Mock the `anypoint-mq:subscriber` (set test event payload + `attributes.properties`); mock all downstream `http:request`; mock `anypoint-mq:publish` to DLQ; mock `module-notification:call-notification-api`.

**Required env-property keys (subset of Section 7):**

- `mq.url`, `mq.region`, `mq.environmentId`, `mq.app.clientId`, `mq.app.clientSecret`
- `mq.queueName`, `mq.dlq.queueName`, `mq.maxLocalMessages`, `mq.connectionTimeout`
- `mq.reconnection.frequency`, `mq.reconnection.attempts`
- `mq.subscriber.circuitBreaker.tripTimeout`, `mq.subscriber.circuitBreaker.errorsThreshold`
- `notification.api.host`, `notification.api.basePath`, `notification.api.clientId`, `notification.api.clientSecret`
- For each downstream: same as 3.1
- `logger.*` keys

**When to choose:** Process-layer APIs consuming asynchronous events delivered via Anypoint MQ where consumer-driven processing is needed and DLQ + retry + circuit-breaker are required.

**Reference Template (if available in this workspace):** `agents/develop/templates/mq-proc-api-template/`
Scaffold keys: MQ subscriber main flow, `common-log-integration-error-details-sub-flow`, `responding-ack-sub-flow`, two-branch error handler (propagate for NACK / continue for ACK).
Use as the skeleton when the Jira story is event-driven and consumes from Anypoint MQ.

