### 3.3 Salesforce Pub/Sub Event App (exp API)

**Trigger:**

```xml
<salesforce-pub-sub:subscribe-channel-listener doc:name="Subscribe channel listener"
    config-ref="salesforce-pubsub_config"
    channelName="${streaming.channel}"
    eventBatchSize="${pubSub.batchsize}">
    <salesforce-pub-sub:replay-option>
        <salesforce-pub-sub:replay-id-from-object-store
            osName="lastreplayId_Object_store" osKey="replayIdSub"/>
    </salesforce-pub-sub:replay-option>
</salesforce-pub-sub:subscribe-channel-listener>
```

**Main flow shape — `{event}-fetch-events-flow`:**

```xml
<flow name="{event}-fetch-events-flow"
      maxConcurrency="${flow.maxConcurrency}"
      initialState="${fetch.events.flow.initialState}">
    <salesforce-pub-sub:subscribe-channel-listener doc:name="Subscribe channel listener"
        config-ref="salesforce-pubsub_config"
        channelName="${streaming.channel}"
        eventBatchSize="${pubSub.batchsize}">
        <salesforce-pub-sub:replay-option>
            <salesforce-pub-sub:replay-id-from-object-store
                osName="lastreplayId_Object_store" osKey="replayIdSub"/>
        </salesforce-pub-sub:replay-option>
    </salesforce-pub-sub:subscribe-channel-listener>
    <set-variable variableName="correlationId" value="#[correlationId]" doc:name="Set correlationId" />
    <ee:transform doc:name="Set Initial Vars">
        <ee:message />
        <ee:variables>
            <ee:set-variable resource="dwls/p-initial-vars.dwl" variableName="initialVar" />
        </ee:variables>
    </ee:transform>
    <flow-ref name="{event}-process-sub-flow"/>
    <error-handler ref="global-error-handler"/>
</flow>
```

**Context variable:** `vars.initialVar` — set via `dwls/p-initial-vars.dwl` (see Section 15). For Pub/Sub events, `entityDetails` is typically empty — set to `null` or omit object keys.

**Required global configs in `global-config.xml`:**

- `salesforce-pubsub_config` — `salesforce-pub-sub:config` with JWT auth (keystore, consumerKey, principal, audienceUrl, tokenUrl)
- `lastreplayId_Object_store` — `objectstore:object-store`
- `custom-logger-connector_config`
- `azure-key-vault-properties-provider_config`
- One or more `http-{target}-server_http-request_config` per downstream system
- `notification-connector_config` — `module-notification:config` (recommended; see Section 11 for the required self-closing XML declaration and property keys)

**Outbound calls:** Same pattern as 3.1 — set `vars.targetApiParams` via DWL, then `flow-ref` to `{downstream-sys-api}-request-flow` (per-system named flow with static `config-ref`). See Section 9.

**Error handling:** Per-event `error-handler ref="global-error-handler"` prevents the event stream from stalling. The global handler logs the error and either does not advance `replayId` (so the event is replayed on next consume cycle) or routes to a DLQ topic. Notification on critical failure. See Section 12.

**Retry / idempotency:** Replay-id from Object Store enables resume on restart. Reconnect on the subscriber. **Idempotency:** dedupe by `payload.event.replayId` (or business key) using Object Store.

**Health check expectation:** Optional. App has no HTTP listener; if exposing health is required, use a separate scheduler-driven `http:listener` flow.

**MUnit mock surface:** Mock `salesforce-pub-sub:subscribe-channel-listener` (inject test event payload); mock all downstream `http:request` and `salesforce:*` operations; mock `os:store` and `os:retrieve`.

**Required env-property keys (subset of Section 7):**

- Salesforce JWT: `sfl.keystore`, `sfl.tokenUrl`, `sfl.audienceUrl`, `sfl.consumerkey`, `sfl.principal`, `sfl.storepassword`, `sfl.certalias`
- `streaming.channel`, `pubSub.batchsize`, `flow.maxConcurrency`, `fetch.events.flow.initialState`
- For each downstream: same as 3.1
- `logger.*` keys

**When to choose:** Experience-layer APIs consuming Salesforce Platform Events / Change Data Capture (CDC) via the Pub/Sub API; need replay-id semantics and event-stream resumption on restart.

**Reference Template (if available in this workspace):** `agents/develop/templates/sf-pubsub-exp-api-template/`
Scaffold keys: `{event}-fetch-events-flow` with `salesforce-pub-sub:subscribe-channel-listener`, replay-id ObjectStore, `{event}-process-sub-flow`, DLQ publish, optional notification.
Use as the skeleton when the Jira story subscribes to Salesforce Platform Events or CDC.

