## 4. Project Structure & Output Location

### Output Location

- **Generate all new API projects** under the `generated-projects/` folder at the workspace root.
- Path pattern: `generated-projects/{project-name}/` (e.g., `generated-projects/sf-http-sys-api-template/`).

### Folder Hierarchy

Generate this structure inside `generated-projects/{project-name}/src/main/mule/`:

```
generated-projects/{project-name}/
├── pom.xml
└── src/main/mule/
    ├── {api-spec}.xml                # Main API flow + APIKit router (e.g., sf-http-sys-api-template.xml)
    ├── implementation/               # Business logic flows
    │   └── *.xml                     # Lower-case-hyphenated flow files
    └── common/                       # Shared configuration and handlers
        ├── global-config.xml         # All global elements (HTTP, connectors, APIKit, logger)
        ├── global-error-handler.xml  # Centralized error handler
        ├── common-connectivity.xml   # Shared flows (optional)
        └── common-utility.xml        # Notification, DLQ, success-response (if needed)
```

### Key Rules

- **Interface vs. logic separation:** Main API flow in root spec file; implementation in `implementation/` subfolder.
- **Global elements:** ALL global configurations (HTTP Listener, connectors, APIKit, module-logger, validation) must be in `global-config.xml` only. **No config elements in implementation flow files.**
- **Flow file names:** All lower-case, hyphenated (e.g., `fetch-data-sf-composite-api.xml`, `global-error-handler.xml`).

