## 8. Logger Configuration and Usage (Insulet Custom Logger Connector)

### Logger config naming and attributes

- **Config name:** `custom-logger-connector_config` (hyphens, not underscores).
- **Required attributes:** `sensitiveKeyParts`, `safeKeys`, `encryptionKey` — all via `${...}` property placeholder syntax:
  - `sensitiveKeyParts="${logger.sensitiveKeyParts}"`
  - `safeKeys="${logger.safeKeys}"`
  - `encryptionKey="${logger.encryptionKey}"`

> **Why `${...}` and not `#[p()]`:** These attributes are evaluated at module-config load time, not at flow-execution time. Using `${...}` resolves the value through the Mule properties-provider chain (including Azure Key Vault) during deployment. `#[p('..')]` is a DataWeave expression that fires at runtime and will not work correctly in connector config elements.

### Properties (config.properties)

- `logger.category` — e.g. `{api-name}-${mule.env}`
- `logger.sensitiveKeyParts` — comma-separated keys to mask (e.g. name, email, ssn, token, password)
- `logger.safeKeys` — comma-separated keys that are safe to log in plain text. Always include standard tracking keys (`requestId,traceId,correlationId`); append app-specific non-PII entity IDs (e.g. `accountId,recordId,campaignName`) relevant to the given integration.
- `logger.encryptionKey` — from secure vault (e.g. Azure Key Vault) in env-specific configs

### Context variable per pattern (from §3)

- **Pattern 3.1 (HTTP listener APIs):** Use `vars.requestContext` set in main flow via `dwls/v-request-context.dwl` before the APIKit router. All loggers use `sourceSystem="#[vars.requestContext.sourceSystem]"` and `targetSystem="#[vars.requestContext.targetSystem]"`.
- **Patterns 3.2 (MQ consumer) and 3.3 (Pub/Sub):** Use `vars.initialVar` set via `dwls/p-initial-vars.dwl`. All loggers use `sourceSystem="#[vars.initialVar.sourceSystem]"`, `targetSystem="#[vars.initialVar.targetSystem]"`, and `entityDetails="#[vars.initialVar.entityDetails default null]"`.

### Logger operations (no deprecated `module-logger:logger`)

- **INFO / general logs:** `module-logger:build-log-without-payload` (no raw payload).
- **DEBUG / payload logs:** `module-logger:build-log-with-encrypted-payload` (masked/encrypted only).
- **Error logs:** `module-logger:build-error-log-with-encrypted-payload` (with `module-logger:body` for `vars.requestContext.originalPayload` or `vars.initialVar.originalPayload`) and `module-logger:build-error-log-without-payload`.

> **CRITICAL — exact operation names:** The Insulet Custom Logger Connector operations do **NOT** have an `info-` infix. The correct names are exactly `build-log-without-payload`, `build-log-with-encrypted-payload`, `build-error-log-without-payload`, `build-error-log-with-encrypted-payload`. Using `build-info-log-*` is wrong and will cause a deployment failure.

```xml
<!-- CORRECT -->
<module-logger:build-log-without-payload doc:name="LOG ENTRY" doc:id="..."
    config-ref="custom-logger-connector_config"
    message="put:\providers\accounts\(id)"
    sourceSystem="#[vars.requestContext.sourceSystem]"
    targetSystem="#[vars.requestContext.targetSystem]" />

<!-- WRONG — do not use -->
<!-- <module-logger:build-info-log-without-payload ... /> -->
```

### Operations reference

| Operation | Level | Use Case |
|-----------|-------|----------|
| `build-log-without-payload` | INFO | Flow milestones, entry/exit logs — no payload |
| `build-log-with-masked-payload` | DEBUG | Debugging with sensitive fields masked |
| `build-log-with-encrypted-payload` | DEBUG | Full encrypted payload for compliance/audit |
| `build-error-log-without-payload` | INFO/ERROR | Error context without payload |
| `build-error-log-with-masked-payload` | DEBUG | Error with masked payload |
| `build-error-log-with-encrypted-payload` | DEBUG | Error with encrypted payload |

### Tracepoint

Valid tracepoint values are a fixed enum. **Do NOT invent short-forms — only the values below are recognised by the Insulet Custom Logger Connector:**

| Tracepoint value | When to use |
|-----------------|-------------|
| `FLOW_START` | First log inside any APIKit flow — entry to the flow |
| `FLOW_END` | Last log in a flow or sub-flow — exit log |
| `BEFORE_HTTP_REQUEST` | Encrypted log immediately **before** the `flow-ref` to a connectivity flow |
| `AFTER_HTTP_REQUEST` | Encrypted log immediately **after** the `flow-ref` to a connectivity flow |
| `APPLICATION_EVENT` | Business milestone log inside a flow (not HTTP-request-related) |
| `EXCEPTION` | All error-handler log entries |

> **INVALID short-forms — do NOT use:** `BEFORE`, `AFTER`, `END`, `START`, `ERROR`. These are not recognised and will cause incorrect log categorisation or connector failure.

- **Exit / flow-end logs:** Use `tracepoint="FLOW_END"` (not `END`).
- **Error handlers:** Use `tracepoint="EXCEPTION"`.
- **Outbound HTTP request:** Use `tracepoint="BEFORE_HTTP_REQUEST"` before, `tracepoint="AFTER_HTTP_REQUEST"` after.

### Mandatory: Before and after outbound API call (encrypted DEBUG logs)

- **Rule:** For every sub-flow that makes an outbound HTTP/API call, add `module-logger:build-log-with-encrypted-payload` **before** and **after** the `flow-ref` to the connectivity flow.
- **Before:** Log the request payload (e.g., `vars.targetApiParams.requestPayload`, or a pre-processed variable like `vars.leadRequestPayload`) with a descriptive message and `tracepoint="BEFORE_HTTP_REQUEST"`.
- **After:** Log the response payload with `tracepoint="AFTER_HTTP_REQUEST"` and a descriptive message.
- **Placement rule — calling sub-flow, NOT inside the connectivity flow:** The connectivity flow (`{downstream-sys-api}-request-flow` / `common-http-request-flow`) is a shared reusable flow. Adding logs inside it would duplicate them for every caller. The encrypted logs must bracket the `<flow-ref>` in the business sub-flow:

```xml
<!-- In the CALLING sub-flow — before the flow-ref -->
<module-logger:build-log-with-encrypted-payload doc:name="LOG BEFORE REQUEST - {operation}"
    config-ref="custom-logger-connector_config"
    message="Invoking {downstream-system} for {operation}"
    tracepoint="BEFORE_HTTP_REQUEST"
    sourceSystem="#[vars.requestContext.sourceSystem]"
    targetSystem="#[vars.requestContext.targetSystem]">
    <module-logger:body><![CDATA[#[output application/json --- vars.targetApiParams.requestPayload default {}]]]></module-logger:body>
</module-logger:build-log-with-encrypted-payload>

<flow-ref name="{downstream-sys-api}-request-flow"
    doc:name="{downstream-sys-api}-request-flow ({operation})"
    target="{operationResponse}" />

<!-- In the CALLING sub-flow — after the flow-ref -->
<!-- When target= is used the response is in vars.{operationResponse}; without target= it is in payload -->
<module-logger:build-log-with-encrypted-payload doc:name="LOG AFTER REQUEST - {operation}"
    config-ref="custom-logger-connector_config"
    message="Response from {downstream-system} for {operation}"
    tracepoint="AFTER_HTTP_REQUEST"
    sourceSystem="#[vars.requestContext.sourceSystem]"
    targetSystem="#[vars.requestContext.targetSystem]">
    <module-logger:body><![CDATA[#[output application/json --- vars.{operationResponse} default payload]]]></module-logger:body>
</module-logger:build-log-with-encrypted-payload>
```

- **Apply to:** POST, PUT, and other endpoints that call downstream APIs. **Exclude:** ping, health-check, and similar read-only health endpoints — these do not need `BEFORE_HTTP_REQUEST` / `AFTER_HTTP_REQUEST` outbound-call logs because they make no business-logic HTTP calls.
- **Important — ping and health-check still require standard entry/exit logs:** The exclusion above applies **only** to the `BEFORE_HTTP_REQUEST` / `AFTER_HTTP_REQUEST` encrypted payload logs. Every APIKit flow — including `GET /ping` and `GET /health-check` — must still have an INFO `build-log-without-payload` entry logger (tracepoint defaults to `FLOW_START`) and an INFO `build-log-without-payload` exit logger with `tracepoint="FLOW_END"`. See Section 10 for canonical shapes.
- **For endpoints without outbound API (stub):** Add before/after logs for the inbound request and outbound response to maintain consistency and aid debugging.

### MUnit tests

- When flow-ref'ing directly to API flows (bypassing main flow), set `requestContext` (Pattern 3.1) or `initialVar` (Patterns 3.2, 3.3) via `munit:variable` before the flow-ref.

