## 9. Common HTTP Connectivity (Outbound)

### Connectivity flow pattern

- **File:** `src/main/mule/common/common-connectivity.xml` — one named request flow per downstream system.
- **Flow naming:** `{downstream-sys-api}-request-flow` — one flow per downstream system, no shared generic flow.
- **Purpose:** Encapsulates outbound HTTP request with retry, before/after logging, and error handling for a specific downstream system.
- **Config ref:** Each named flow has a **static** `config-ref="{downstream-sys-api}_http-request_config"`. Do NOT use a dynamic MEL expression for `config-ref` — Mule 4 resolves this attribute at deploy time, not at runtime. Using `#[vars.httpRequestConfigRef ...]` will not work.

### Required variables before flow-ref

- **`targetApiParams`** — set via a `v-set-target-api-params-*.dwl` file; complete canonical structure:
  ```
  {
    requestMethod:   string,       // HTTP verb (GET, POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE)
    requestPath:     string,       // URI path; use /{param} placeholders mapped via uriParams
    requestProtocol: string,       // "HTTP" or "HTTPS"
    requestHost:     string,       // resolved from property (e.g. Mule::p('sfl.crm.host'))
    requestPort:     string,       // resolved from property (e.g. Mule::p('sfl.crm.port'))
    requestBasePath: string,       // resolved from property (e.g. Mule::p('sfl.crm.basePath'))
    requestPayload:  object|array, // outbound body; empty object {} for GET/DELETE
    headers?:        object,       // x-request-id, client_id, client_secret, sourceSystem, targetSystem
    uriParams?:      object,       // URI template variables (e.g. { id: vars.accountId })
    queryParams?:    object        // optional query string parameters
  }
  ```
- **Usage:** Caller sets `vars.targetApiParams` via the DWL transform then `flow-ref`s to `{downstream-sys-api}-request-flow`. No `httpRequestConfigRef` variable is needed or used.

### DWL file references in ee:transform

> **CRITICAL — `resource=` attribute, never `${file::...}`:** DWL files must always be referenced using the `resource=` attribute on `ee:set-variable` and `ee:set-payload`. The `${file::dwls/...}` Spring property placeholder inside CDATA is **not** equivalent and will not load the DWL at runtime.

```xml
<!-- CORRECT: resource= attribute on ee:set-variable -->
<ee:transform doc:name="FV Set targetApiParams" doc:id="...">
    <ee:message />
    <ee:variables>
        <ee:set-variable resource="dwls/v-targetApiParams-sfl-crm-persona-sys-api.dwl"
            variableName="targetApiParams" />
    </ee:variables>
</ee:transform>

<!-- CORRECT: resource= attribute on ee:set-payload -->
<ee:transform doc:name="DW Set Response" doc:id="...">
    <ee:message>
        <ee:set-payload resource="dwls/p-update-provider-response.dwl" />
    </ee:message>
</ee:transform>

<!-- WRONG — do not use ${file::...} -->
<!--
<ee:set-variable variableName="targetApiParams">
    <![CDATA[${file::dwls/v-targetApiParams-sfl-crm-persona-sys-api.dwl}]]>
</ee:set-variable>
-->
```

### Component naming

- All processors and scopes must have descriptive `doc:name` (no default Studio names like "Retry", "Try").
- Flow-ref doc:name: "Flow Reference to {target-sub-flow-name}".

### Flow structure

- `until-successful` with `${retry.attempts}` and `${retry.interval}`.
- `try` with `http:request` using a **static** `config-ref="{downstream-sys-api}_http-request_config"`.
- Inner error-handler: `on-error-propagate` for `${httpErrors}`, `on-error-continue` for others — both set `vars.success = false` and `vars.errorDetails = error`.
- After `until-successful`: `flow-ref` to `check-for-raise-error-sub-flow`.
- Outer error-handler: `on-error-propagate` type `ANY` — LOG ERROR (without payload).
- **No LOG BEFORE/AFTER in the connectivity flow itself.** The encrypted `BEFORE_HTTP_REQUEST` and `AFTER_HTTP_REQUEST` logs must be placed in the **calling sub-flow** around the `<flow-ref>` to this connectivity flow. See §8 "Mandatory: Before and after outbound API call" for the canonical pattern.

> Add one named flow per downstream system. Do NOT share a single flow across systems using a dynamic `config-ref`.

> **`http:success-status-code-validator` — do NOT add inside `until-successful`:** Non-2xx HTTP responses must propagate as typed `HTTP:*` errors (e.g. `HTTP:NOT_FOUND`, `HTTP:SERVICE_UNAVAILABLE`) so the inner `on-error-propagate type="${httpErrors}"` can classify them correctly for retry, and so `customErrors.dwl` can map them to the right HTTP status. Adding `<http:success-status-code-validator>` collapses all non-2xx into `HTTP:BAD_REQUEST`, which defeats this classification. The validator is only appropriate for calls made outside a retry scope where you need explicit status-code gating.

### Canonical `{downstream-sys-api}-request-flow` (embedded)

```xml
<!-- common-connectivity.xml — one flow per downstream system -->
<!-- NOTE: Do NOT add LOG BEFORE/AFTER here. Those encrypted logs belong in the CALLING sub-flow,
     bracketing the flow-ref to this flow. See §8 for the canonical calling-sub-flow pattern. -->
<flow name="{downstream-sys-api}-request-flow" doc:name="{downstream-sys-api}-request-flow">
    <until-successful maxRetries="${retry.attempts}" millisBetweenRetries="${retry.interval}" doc:name="Retry">
        <try doc:name="Try Outbound Request">
            <http:request
                method="#[vars.targetApiParams.requestMethod]"
                path="#[vars.targetApiParams.requestPath]"
                config-ref="{downstream-sys-api}_http-request_config"
                doc:name="REQUEST {downstream-sys-api}"
                sendCorrelationId="ALWAYS">
                <http:body><![CDATA[#[vars.targetApiParams.requestPayload]]]></http:body>
                <http:headers><![CDATA[#[vars.targetApiParams.headers default {}]]]></http:headers>
                <http:uri-params><![CDATA[#[vars.targetApiParams.uriParams default {}]]]></http:uri-params>
                <http:query-params><![CDATA[#[vars.targetApiParams.queryParams default {}]]]></http:query-params>
            </http:request>
            <ee:transform doc:name="FV Set Success = true, Error = null">
                <ee:message />
                <ee:variables>
                    <ee:set-variable variableName="success"><![CDATA[true]]></ee:set-variable>
                    <ee:set-variable variableName="errorDetails"><![CDATA[null]]></ee:set-variable>
                </ee:variables>
            </ee:transform>
            <error-handler>
                <on-error-propagate type="${httpErrors}" doc:name="On Error Propagate (Retry)">
                    <ee:transform doc:name="FV Set Success = false, Error Details">
                        <ee:message />
                        <ee:variables>
                            <ee:set-variable variableName="success"><![CDATA[false]]></ee:set-variable>
                            <ee:set-variable variableName="errorDetails"><![CDATA[%dw 2.0
output application/java
---
error]]></ee:set-variable>
                        </ee:variables>
                    </ee:transform>
                </on-error-propagate>
                <on-error-continue doc:name="On Error Continue (Non-Retryable)">
                    <ee:transform doc:name="FV Set Success = false, Error Details">
                        <ee:message />
                        <ee:variables>
                            <ee:set-variable variableName="success"><![CDATA[false]]></ee:set-variable>
                            <ee:set-variable variableName="errorDetails"><![CDATA[%dw 2.0
output application/java
---
error]]></ee:set-variable>
                        </ee:variables>
                    </ee:transform>
                </on-error-continue>
            </error-handler>
        </try>
    </until-successful>
    <flow-ref doc:name="Flow Reference to check-for-raise-error-sub-flow"
        name="check-for-raise-error-sub-flow" />
    <error-handler>
        <on-error-propagate type="ANY" doc:name="On Error Propagate">
            <module-logger:build-error-log-without-payload
                doc:name="LOG ERROR"
                config-ref="custom-logger-connector_config"
                message="{downstream-sys-api} request failed"
                logLevel="ERROR"
                tracepoint="EXCEPTION"
                sourceSystem="#[vars.requestContext.sourceSystem]"
                targetSystem="#[vars.requestContext.targetSystem]"
                entityDetails="#[vars.requestContext.entityDetails default null]"
                errorType='#[(vars.errorDetails.errorType.namespace default "UNKNOWN") ++ ":" ++ (vars.errorDetails.errorType.identifier default "UNKNOWN")]'
                errorDescription='#[vars.errorDetails.description default "Unhandled error"]'
                cause='#[vars.errorDetails.cause.message default ""]'
                errorCode="#[vars.errorDetails.cause.errorMessage.attributes.statusCode default 500]" />
        </on-error-propagate>
    </error-handler>
</flow>
```

### `connectivity-error-handler-sub-flow`

- **Sub-flow name:** `connectivity-error-handler-sub-flow` (suffix `-sub-flow` per naming conventions).
- **Placement:** Defined in `global-error-handler.xml`.
- **Behavior:** Choice on `!vars.success` → raise `APP:CONNECTIVITY_FAILED` with `vars.errorDetails.description`.

```xml
<sub-flow name="connectivity-error-handler-sub-flow">
    <choice doc:name="CHECK for Success == false">
        <when expression="#[!vars.success default false]">
            <raise-error doc:name="RAISE APP:CONNECTIVITY_FAILED"
                type="APP:CONNECTIVITY_FAILED"
                description='#[vars.errorDetails.description default error.detailedDescription default ""]' />
        </when>
    </choice>
</sub-flow>
```

### HTTP request config

- **Naming:** `{downstream-sys-api}_http-request_config` (end with `_config`).
- **Placement:** `global-config.xml`.
- **Properties:** `{target}.host`, `{target}.port`, `{target}.basePath` for each downstream system. No shared `config-ref` property — each system has its own named config.
- **Include only configs in use:** Define HTTP request configs only for targets the API calls. Remove unused configs and their properties from all env config files.

### Config properties (config-{env}.properties)

- **Mandatory in all env configs:** `logger.encryptionKey=${azure-key-vault-properties-provider::secret::logger-encryption-key}`
- **Outbound targets (examples):** Add only properties for targets the API calls. Example for a token server: `token.host`, `token.port`, `token.basePath`, `token.path`; Azure keys: `token.clientId`, `token.clientSecret` via `na-{api}-token-*` secret naming.
- **Azure Key Vault naming:** `${azure-key-vault-properties-provider::secret::<secret-name>}`; API-specific secrets use `na-{api}-{context}-{key}` (e.g. `na-{api-name}-token-client-id`).

### Error log DWL (`p-set-error-log-original-request.dwl`)

- Uses `vars.requestContext` and `vars.targetApiParams`.
- Outputs `originalRequest` with method, requestPath, queryParams, uriParams, body (when present).
- Prefers `targetApiParams` for outbound request details; falls back to `requestContext` for inbound.

### Multi-Target HTTP Connectivity

#### Per-system named flows

- **Rule:** Create one named request flow per downstream system in `common-connectivity.xml`. Each flow has a **static** `config-ref` pointing to that system's `http:request-config`.
- **Config selection:** Callers set `vars.targetApiParams` via a `v-set-target-api-params-*.dwl` file, then `flow-ref` to `{downstream-sys-api}-request-flow`.
- **Example:** `create-record-sub-flow` sets `vars.targetApiParams` via `v-set-target-api-params-sf-object.dwl` then calls `flow-ref name="{downstream-sys-api}-request-flow"`.
- **Placement:** One named flow per downstream system in `common-connectivity.xml`.

#### Pass-through inbound auth

- **Rule:** When calling downstream APIs that require JWT/Authorization, pass the inbound Authorization header in `targetApiParams.headers`.
- **DWL:** `"Authorization": vars.requestContext.headers.Authorization default vars.requestContext.headers.authorization default ""`
- **Example use case:** `{exp-api}` POST `/records` → `{proc-api}` (JWT validated at gateway; header forwarded to downstream).

#### Request pre-processing before outbound call

- **Rule:** When the outbound payload must be transformed before the HTTP call, store the result in a variable first.
- **Pattern:** `ee:set-variable variableName="{resourceName}RequestPayload" resource="dwls/p-{resource}-request-merge.dwl"`; then `v-{resource}-api-params.dwl` references `vars.{resourceName}RequestPayload default payload`.
- **Reason:** Keeps targetApiParams DWL simple and reusable.

