## 10. Health Check & Readiness

- **When the API has downstream HTTP dependencies** (process APIs calling sys APIs): Implement `health-check-ready-sub-flow` (or `healthcheck-ready-sub-flow`) using `scatter-gather` to call each downstream system's `/health-check` endpoint via the existing common-connectivity HTTP request flows.
- Use `v-targetApiParams-{system}-healthcheck.dwl` per downstream system to set `requestMethod`, `requestPath`, `host`, `basePath`, etc. from properties (e.g. `{system}.healthCheck.method`, `{system}.healthCheck.path`).
- Use `on-error-continue` per route to set payload to `{ apiName, status: message.systemDown }` on failure.
- Use `p-set-readiness-response-success.dwl` (or equivalent) to aggregate scatter-gather results into `{ apiName, version, correlationId, timestamp, dependencies[], status }`.
- **When the API has no downstream HTTP dependencies** (e.g. sys APIs): Use a simple readiness flow (e.g. check internal dependency like Salesforce via `get-timestamp-sub-flow`) and `p-set-readiness-response.dwl` with dependencies if applicable.

### Canonical `GET /ping` APIKit flow (embedded)

Every HTTP Listener API must expose a `GET /ping` liveness endpoint. The APIKit-generated flow follows the standard entry + set-payload + exit log shape — no outbound HTTP calls, no BEFORE/AFTER_HTTP_REQUEST logs.

```xml
<flow name="get:\ping:{api-spec}_config">
    <module-logger:build-log-without-payload doc:name="LOG ENTRY"
        config-ref="custom-logger-connector_config"
        message="GET /ping"
        sourceSystem="#[vars.requestContext.sourceSystem]"
        targetSystem="#[vars.requestContext.targetSystem]" />
    <ee:transform doc:name="DW Set Aliveness Response">
        <ee:message>
            <ee:set-payload resource="dwls/p-set-liveness-response.dwl" />
        </ee:message>
    </ee:transform>
    <module-logger:build-log-without-payload doc:name="LOG EXIT"
        config-ref="custom-logger-connector_config"
        message="GET /ping"
        tracepoint="FLOW_END"
        sourceSystem="#[vars.requestContext.sourceSystem]"
        targetSystem="#[vars.requestContext.targetSystem]" />
</flow>
```

### Canonical `GET /health-check` APIKit flow (embedded)

Every HTTP Listener API must expose a `GET /health-check` readiness endpoint. The flow delegates all logic to `health-check-ready-sub-flow` and wraps it with standard entry/exit logs.

```xml
<flow name="get:\health-check:{api-spec}_config">
    <module-logger:build-log-without-payload doc:name="LOG ENTRY"
        config-ref="custom-logger-connector_config"
        message="GET /health-check"
        sourceSystem="#[vars.requestContext.sourceSystem]"
        targetSystem="#[vars.requestContext.targetSystem]" />
    <flow-ref doc:name="Flow Reference to health-check-ready-sub-flow" name="health-check-ready-sub-flow" />
    <module-logger:build-log-without-payload doc:name="LOG EXIT"
        config-ref="custom-logger-connector_config"
        message="GET /health-check"
        tracepoint="FLOW_END"
        sourceSystem="#[vars.requestContext.sourceSystem]"
        targetSystem="#[vars.requestContext.targetSystem]" />
</flow>
```

### Canonical `health-check-ready-sub-flow` (embedded)

```xml
<sub-flow name="health-check-ready-sub-flow">
    <scatter-gather doc:name="Send request to all downstream systems">
        <route>
            <try doc:name="Try {system-a} Health Check">
                <ee:transform doc:name="{system-a} Healthcheck Parameters">
                    <ee:message />
                    <ee:variables>
                        <ee:set-variable resource="dwls/v-targetApiParams-{system-a}-healthcheck.dwl" variableName="targetApiParams" />
                    </ee:variables>
                </ee:transform>
                <flow-ref doc:name="Flow Reference to {system-a}-request-flow ({system-a} health-check)" name="{system-a}-request-flow" />
                <ee:transform doc:name="Normalize {system-a} success response">
                    <ee:message>
                        <ee:set-payload><![CDATA[%dw 2.0
output application/json
---
{
    apiName: "{system-a}",
    status: payload.status default p('message.systemUp')
}]]></ee:set-payload>
                    </ee:message>
                </ee:transform>
                <error-handler>
                    <on-error-continue enableNotifications="true" logException="true" doc:name="On Error Continue">
                        <ee:transform doc:name="Set {system-a} status down">
                            <ee:message>
                                <ee:set-payload><![CDATA[%dw 2.0
output application/json
---
{
    apiName: "{system-a}",
    status: p('message.systemDown')
}]]></ee:set-payload>
                            </ee:message>
                        </ee:transform>
                    </on-error-continue>
                </error-handler>
            </try>
        </route>
        <route>
            <try doc:name="Try {system-b} Health Check">
                <ee:transform doc:name="{system-b} Healthcheck Parameters">
                    <ee:message />
                    <ee:variables>
                        <ee:set-variable resource="dwls/v-targetApiParams-{system-b}-healthcheck.dwl" variableName="targetApiParams" />
                    </ee:variables>
                </ee:transform>
                <flow-ref doc:name="Flow Reference to {system-b}-request-flow ({system-b} health-check)" name="{system-b}-request-flow" />
                <ee:transform doc:name="Normalize {system-b} success response">
                    <ee:message>
                        <ee:set-payload><![CDATA[%dw 2.0
output application/json
---
{
    apiName: "{system-b}",
    status: payload.status default p('message.systemUp')
}]]></ee:set-payload>
                    </ee:message>
                </ee:transform>
                <error-handler>
                    <on-error-continue enableNotifications="true" logException="true" doc:name="On Error Continue">
                        <ee:transform doc:name="Set {system-b} status down">
                            <ee:message>
                                <ee:set-payload><![CDATA[%dw 2.0
output application/json
---
{
    apiName: "{system-b}",
    status: p('message.systemDown')
}]]></ee:set-payload>
                            </ee:message>
                        </ee:transform>
                    </on-error-continue>
                </error-handler>
            </try>
        </route>
    </scatter-gather>
    <ee:transform doc:name="DW Set Readiness Response">
        <ee:message>
            <ee:set-payload resource="dwls/p-set-readiness-response-success.dwl" />
        </ee:message>
    </ee:transform>
    <module-logger:build-log-without-payload doc:name="Log Healthcheck result"
        config-ref="custom-logger-connector_config"
        message="#[output application/json --- if(payload.status != p('message.systemsReady')) &quot;health check unsuccessful&quot; else &quot;health check successful&quot;]"
        tracepoint="APPLICATION_EVENT"
        sourceSystem="#[vars.requestContext.sourceSystem]"
        targetSystem="#[vars.requestContext.targetSystem]" />
</sub-flow>
```

### Canonical `dwls/v-targetApiParams-{system}-healthcheck.dwl` (embedded)

```dwl
%dw 2.0
output application/json
---
{
    "host": Mule::p("{system}.host"),
    "basePath": Mule::p("{system}.basePath") default "/",
    "requestMethod": Mule::p("{system}.healthCheck.method"),
    "requestPath": Mule::p("{system}.healthCheck.path"),
    "headers": {
        "x-correlation-id": correlationId,
        "client_id": Mule::p('{system}.client_id'),
        "client_secret": Mule::p('{system}.client_secret'),
        "sourceSystem": Mule::p('app.name'),
        "targetSystem": Mule::p('targetSystem')
    },
    "uriParams": {},
    "queryParams": {},
    "requestPayload": {}
}
```

### Canonical `dwls/p-set-readiness-response-success.dwl` (embedded)

```dwl
%dw 2.0
import * from dw::core::Arrays
output application/json
var statusValue = if ((payload pluck (value, key, index) -> (value.payload default value).status)
    some (($ != p('message.systemUp')) and ($ != p('message.systemsReady')))
) p('message.systemsNotReady') else p('message.systemsReady')
---
{
    apiName: p('app.name'),
    version: p('app.version'),
    correlationId: correlationId,
    timestamp: now() >> p('timezone'),
    dependencies: (payload pluck {
        "name": ($.payload.apiName default $.payload.name default $.apiName default $.name),
        "status": ($.payload default $).status
    }),
    status: statusValue
}
```

### Pattern applicability

- **3.1 HTTP Listener API:** Both `GET /ping` (liveness) and `GET /health-check` (readiness) endpoints required.
- **3.2 Anypoint MQ Consumer:** No HTTP listener; readiness is optional. If exposed, use a separate scheduler-driven flow.
- **3.3 Salesforce Pub/Sub Event App:** Same as 3.2 — readiness is optional and exposed via a separate listener flow if required.

