## 11. Notification Connector (`send-notification-sub-flow`)

- The `send-notification-sub-flow` must use **`module-notification:call-notification-api`** (not `module-notification:send`).
- Use `module-notification:http-body` — JSON from `vars.notificationInputBody` (built by `v-notification-input-body.dwl`).
- Use `module-notification:http-headers` — `x-correlation-id`, `client_id`, `client_secret` from properties.
- Add `notification.api.clientId` and `notification.api.clientSecret` to required properties when notification is enabled.

### Canonical `module-notification:config` declaration (`global-config.xml`)

**CRITICAL:** The `<module-notification:config>` element **must be declared in `global-config.xml`**. Without this declaration the Mule runtime throws `IllegalArgumentException: There's no <module-notification:config> named [notification-connector_config]` at startup.

**CRITICAL:** Do **NOT** add `host` or `basePath` as XML attributes on `<module-notification:config>`. Connector version `260ebaee:mule-notification-connector:1.0.1` resolves connection details from property placeholders via module defaults only. Adding them causes `cvc-complex-type.3.2.2` schema validation failures at deploy time.

```xml
<!-- global-config.xml — self-closing, NO host/basePath/port attributes.
     Connection is resolved from property placeholders via module defaults.
     Properties notification.api.host / .port / .basePath must be present
     in every env-specific config file (e.g. config-dev.properties). -->
<module-notification:config name="notification-connector_config" />
```

Required property keys (add to every env config file when notification is enabled):
```properties
notification.api.host=
notification.api.port=443
notification.api.basePath=/notifications
notification.api.clientId=${azure-key-vault-properties-provider::secret::<replace-proper-value>}
notification.api.clientSecret=${azure-key-vault-properties-provider::secret::<replace-proper-value>}
```

### Canonical `send-notification-sub-flow` (embedded)

```xml
<sub-flow name="send-notification-sub-flow">
    <try>
        <ee:transform doc:name="Notification Input Body">
            <ee:message />
            <ee:variables>
                <ee:set-variable resource="dwls/v-notification-input-body.dwl" variableName="notificationInputBody" />
            </ee:variables>
        </ee:transform>
        <module-logger:build-log-with-masked-payload doc:name="Sending notification"
            config-ref="custom-logger-connector_config"
            message="Sending notification through connector"
            tracepoint="BEFORE_HTTP_REQUEST"
            sourceSystem="#[vars.initialVar.sourceSystem]"
            targetSystem="#[vars.initialVar.targetSystem]"
            entityDetails="#[vars.initialVar.entityDetails default null]">
            <module-logger:body><![CDATA[#[output application/json --- vars.notificationInputBody]]]></module-logger:body>
        </module-logger:build-log-with-masked-payload>
        <module-notification:call-notification-api doc:name="Send Error Details" config-ref="notification-connector_config">
            <module-notification:http-body><![CDATA[#[output application/json --- vars.notificationInputBody]]]></module-notification:http-body>
            <module-notification:http-headers><![CDATA[#[output application/json --- {
                'x-correlation-id': correlationId,
                'client_id': p('notification.api.clientId'),
                'client_secret': p('notification.api.clientSecret')
            }]]]></module-notification:http-headers>
        </module-notification:call-notification-api>
        <module-logger:build-log-without-payload doc:name="Notification Sent"
            config-ref="custom-logger-connector_config"
            message="Notification sent successfully"
            tracepoint="AFTER_HTTP_REQUEST"
            sourceSystem="#[vars.initialVar.sourceSystem]"
            targetSystem="#[vars.initialVar.targetSystem]"
            entityDetails="#[vars.initialVar.entityDetails default null]"/>
        <error-handler>
            <on-error-continue doc:name="On Error Continue">
                <module-logger:build-error-log-with-encrypted-payload doc:name="LOG ERROR"
                    config-ref="custom-logger-connector_config"
                    message="Error sending notification"
                    logLevel="ERROR" tracepoint="EXCEPTION"
                    sourceSystem="#[vars.initialVar.sourceSystem]"
                    targetSystem="#[vars.initialVar.targetSystem]"
                    entityDetails="#[vars.initialVar.entityDetails default null]"
                    cause='#[error.cause.localizedMessage default error.detailedDescription default ""]'
                    errorType='#[(error.errorType.namespace default "UNKNOWN") ++ ":" ++ (error.errorType.identifier default "UNKNOWN")]'
                    errorDescription='#[vars.errorDetails.detailedDescription default error.description default ""]'
                    errorCode="#[vars.errorDetails.cause.errorMessage.attributes.statusCode default 500]">
                    <module-logger:body><![CDATA[#[output application/json ---
{
    error: (vars.errorDetails.description default error.description default "")
}]]]></module-logger:body>
                </module-logger:build-error-log-with-encrypted-payload>
            </on-error-continue>
        </error-handler>
    </try>
</sub-flow>
```

