## 12. Error Handling

### Global Error Handler

- Define a global error handler in `global-error-handler.xml`.
- Reference it from the main API flow using `defaultErrorHandler-ref="global-error-handler"`.
- Use `on-error-continue` to return structured error responses; use `on-error-propagate` in sub-flows to bubble errors up.

### Custom Error Mapping

- Define mappings in `errors/customErrors.dwl` (e.g., `SALESFORCE:CONNECTIVITY` → 503, `MULE:UNKNOWN` → 500).
- Use `module-error-handler-plugin` with `custom-errors` referencing the DWL file.

### Error Handler Logging

- Error handlers must include **two** `module-logger` entries:
  1. **INFO/ERROR** — `build-error-log-without-payload` (category `com.insulet.general`) — error context without payload
  2. **DEBUG** — `build-error-log-with-masked-payload` or `build-error-log-with-encrypted-payload` — protected payload for triage
- **`tracepoint="EXCEPTION"` is required** on all error handler log entries.
- Both entries must include `sourceSystem` and `targetSystem`.

### Structured Error Response

- Standardize error responses. Payload must be JSON with `correlationId`, `status`, `code`, `message`.

### Pattern-specific notes (cross-reference §3)

- **3.1 HTTP Listener API:** `on-error-continue` at the global handler returns the structured error response. HTTP status pulled from `errors/customErrors.dwl`.
- **3.2 Anypoint MQ Consumer:** Per-message `on-error-continue` to prevent message loss; failed messages routed via `publish-to-dlq-sub-flow` (publishes to `${mq.dlq.queueName}`) and `send-notification-sub-flow` (notification on DLQ failure).
- **3.3 Salesforce Pub/Sub Event App:** Per-event `error-handler ref="global-error-handler"` prevents event-stream stall. Replay-id is not advanced for unrecoverable failures; notification on critical failure.

### Canonical `global-error-handler` (embedded)

```xml
<error-handler name="global-error-handler">
    <on-error-continue enableNotifications="true" logException="true" doc:name="On Error Continue">
        <module-error-handler-plugin:process-error doc:name="Process Error"
            error="#[vars.errorDetails default error]" useGeneratedError="false">
            <module-error-handler-plugin:custom-errors><![CDATA[#[${file::errors/customErrors.dwl}]]]></module-error-handler-plugin:custom-errors>
        </module-error-handler-plugin:process-error>
        <set-variable variableName="httpStatus" value="#[attributes.httpStatus]" doc:name="Set HTTP Status Code" />
        <module-logger:build-error-log-with-encrypted-payload doc:name="Log Error"
            config-ref="custom-logger-connector_config"
            message='#[output application/json --- (attributes.httpStatus default "500") ++ " " ++ (payload.error.reason default "Internal Server Error")]'
            logLevel="ERROR" tracepoint="EXCEPTION"
            sourceSystem="#[(vars.requestContext.sourceSystem default vars.initialVar.sourceSystem) default p('sourceSystem')]"
            targetSystem="#[(vars.requestContext.targetSystem default vars.initialVar.targetSystem) default p('targetSystem')]"
            cause='#[error.cause.localizedMessage default error.detailedDescription default ""]'
            errorType='#[(error.errorType.namespace default "UNKNOWN") ++ ":" ++ (error.errorType.identifier default "UNKNOWN")]'
            errorDescription='#[error.description default ""]'
            errorCode='#[vars.httpStatus default "500"]'>
            <module-logger:body><![CDATA[#[(vars.requestContext default vars.initialVar default {}).originalPayload default { code: attributes.httpStatus, message: attributes.errorLog }]]]></module-logger:body>
        </module-logger:build-error-log-with-encrypted-payload>
        <ee:transform doc:name="Set Error Variables">
            <ee:message />
            <ee:variables>
                <ee:set-variable variableName="errorCode"><![CDATA[%dw 2.0
output application/json
---
attributes.httpStatus default 500]]></ee:set-variable>
                <ee:set-variable variableName="errorMessage"><![CDATA[%dw 2.0
output application/json
---
attributes.errorLog default ""]]></ee:set-variable>
            </ee:variables>
        </ee:transform>
        <!-- For Patterns 3.2 and 3.3 only: -->
        <!-- <flow-ref name="send-notification-sub-flow"/> -->
        <!-- <flow-ref name="publish-to-dlq-sub-flow"/> -->
    </on-error-continue>
</error-handler>
```

### Canonical `errors/customErrors.dwl` (embedded)

This is the complete, production-ready canonical — use it verbatim for every new project. Replace `{api-name}` in the JSDoc with the actual API name. For Pattern 3.3 (Salesforce) add the Salesforce-specific block documented below.

```dwl
/**
 * Custom error handling mappings for {api-name}.
 */
%dw 2.0
output application/json
import * from module_error_handler_plugin::common

var previousError = do {
    var nested = [
        error.childErrors..errorMessage.payload,        // Composite (Scatter-Gather, etc.)
        error.suppressedErrors..errorMessage.payload,   // Until-Successful
        error.exception.errorMessage.typedValue         // Standard Error — must be last
    ] dw::core::Arrays::firstWith !isEmpty($)
    ---
    if (nested is Array)
        toString(nested map (toString($)) distinctBy $)
    else
        toString(nested)
}

// Reusable function to extract and format Mule composite routing errors
fun extractRoutingErrors(errorMessage: Any): String =
    // Safely check if it's a string and not empty using the 'is' operator
    if (errorMessage is String and !isEmpty(errorMessage))
        (
            // Explicitly cast to String so the compiler allows splitBy
            ((errorMessage as String) splitBy "\n")
                filter ($ contains "Route")
                map ((line) -> trim(line replace /^.*Exception:\s/ with ""))
        ) joinBy ", " default "No route-specific errors identified"
    else
        "Invalid or missing error message data"
---
{
    "APP:CONNECTIVITY_FAILED": {
        code: 503,
        reason: "Service Unavailable",
        message: if (!isEmpty(previousError)) previousError else error.description
    },
    "HTTP:INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR": {
        code: 500,
        reason: "Internal Server Error",
        message: if (!isEmpty(previousError)) previousError else error.description
    },
    "HTTP:BAD_REQUEST": {
        code: 400,
        reason: "Bad Request",
        message: if (!isEmpty(previousError)) previousError else error.description
    },
    "HTTP:UNAUTHORIZED": {
        code: 401,
        reason: "Unauthorized",
        message: if (!isEmpty(previousError)) previousError else error.description
    },
    "HTTP:NOT_FOUND": {
        code: 404,
        reason: "Not Found",
        message: if (!isEmpty(previousError)) previousError else error.description
    },
    "HTTP:CONNECTIVITY": {
        code: 503,
        reason: "Service Unavailable",
        message: if (!isEmpty(previousError)) previousError else error.description
    },
    "HTTP:SERVICE_UNAVAILABLE": {
        code: 503,
        reason: "Service Unavailable",
        message: if (!isEmpty(previousError)) previousError else error.description
    },
    "HTTP:TIMEOUT": {
        code: 504,
        reason: "Gateway Timeout",
        message: if (!isEmpty(previousError)) previousError else error.description
    },
    "MULE:RETRY_EXHAUSTED": {
        code: 503,
        reason: "Service Unavailable",
        message: if (!isEmpty(previousError)) previousError else error.description
    },
    "MULE:COMPOSITE_ROUTING": {
        code: 500,
        reason: "Internal Server Error",
        message: extractRoutingErrors(if (!isEmpty(previousError)) previousError else error.description)
    },
    "MULE:UNKNOWN": {
        code: error.exception.errorMessage.attributes.statusCode default 500,
        reason: error.exception.errorMessage.attributes.reasonPhrase default "Internal Server Error",
        message: if (!isEmpty(previousError)) previousError else error.description
    }
}
```

> **Pattern 3.3 (Salesforce) additions:** When the API uses a Salesforce connector, add these entries to the map above, before `MULE:UNKNOWN`:
>
> ```dwl
>     "SALESFORCE:CONNECTIVITY": {
>         code: 503,
>         reason: "Service Unavailable",
>         message: if (!isEmpty(previousError)) previousError else error.description
>     },
>     "SALESFORCE:NOT_FOUND": {
>         code: 404,
>         reason: "Not Found",
>         message: if (!isEmpty(previousError)) previousError else error.description
>     },
>     "SALESFORCE:TIMEOUT": {
>         code: 504,
>         reason: "Gateway Timeout",
>         message: if (!isEmpty(previousError)) previousError else error.description
>     },
>     "SALESFORCE:LIMIT_EXCEEDED": {
>         code: 429,
>         reason: "Too Many Requests",
>         message: if (!isEmpty(previousError)) previousError else error.description
>     },
>     "SALESFORCE:INVALID_INPUT": {
>         code: 400,
>         reason: "Bad Request",
>         message: if (!isEmpty(previousError)) previousError else error.description
>     },
> ```

> **Rule:** `MULE:COMPOSITE_ROUTING` **must always be present** when `scatter-gather` is used (e.g., `health-check-ready-sub-flow`). Omitting it causes unhandled 500 errors on scatter-gather failures.

### Async Error Logging Sub-flow (`log-transaction-error-sub-flow`)

- **Rule:** When the global error handler fires an async flow-ref to post transaction errors to a downstream system, that sub-flow's HTTP call **must** be wrapped in `<try>/<on-error-continue>` so that any failure to reach the error-logging endpoint is silently swallowed — it must never surface a new error and must never interrupt the original error response.
- **Why:** Without this guard, a network failure or 5xx from the error-logging endpoint re-raises an error inside `on-error-continue`, which can mask the original error or cause an unexpected 500 response to the client.

```xml
<!-- common-utility.xml -->
<sub-flow name="log-transaction-error-sub-flow" doc:name="log-transaction-error-sub-flow">
    <try doc:name="Try Post Transaction Error">
        <ee:transform doc:name="FV Set targetApiParams for Transaction Error">
            <ee:message />
            <ee:variables>
                <ee:set-variable resource="dwls/v-targetApiParams-transaction-error.dwl" variableName="targetApiParams" />
            </ee:variables>
        </ee:transform>
        <flow-ref name="common-http-request-flow" doc:name="Flow Reference to common-http-request-flow (POST transaction error)" />
        <error-handler>
            <on-error-continue type="ANY" doc:name="On Error Continue (swallow error-logging failures)">
                <module-logger:build-error-log-without-payload doc:name="LOG ERROR - Transaction Error Logging Failed"
                    config-ref="custom-logger-connector_config"
                    message="Failed to post transaction error — swallowed to protect original error response"
                    logLevel="ERROR"
                    tracepoint="EXCEPTION"
                    sourceSystem="#[(vars.requestContext.sourceSystem default vars.initialVar.sourceSystem) default p('sourceSystem')]"
                    targetSystem="#[(vars.requestContext.targetSystem default vars.initialVar.targetSystem) default p('targetSystem')]" />
            </on-error-continue>
        </error-handler>
    </try>
</sub-flow>
```

---



### Reconnection Strategy

- Configure reconnection on all external connectors (DB, HTTP Request, Salesforce, Anypoint MQ).
- Use properties: `reconnection.frequency`, `reconnection.attempts` (e.g., 2000ms, 3 attempts).

```xml
<reconnect frequency="${reconnection.frequency}" count="${reconnection.attempts}" />
```

### Transient Errors

- Use `until-successful` for retryable operations.
- Define transient error types in properties (e.g., `httpErrors`) and use `on-error-propagate` for retries.
- Set `success` and `errorDetails` variables for downstream decision-making; use the `connectivity-error-handler-sub-flow` pattern (Section 9) to raise `APP:CONNECTIVITY_FAILED` when appropriate.
- **Common-connectivity pattern:** `until-successful` → try (HTTP request → set success/errorDetails) → `flow-ref` to `connectivity-error-handler-sub-flow` → `build-log-with-encrypted-payload` BEFORE/AFTER_HTTP_REQUEST. The full canonical XML is embedded in Section 9.

### Per-pattern resilience notes (cross-reference §3)

- **3.1 HTTP Listener API:** `until-successful` retry on `${httpErrors}` for outbound calls. Caller idempotency at gateway / API contract level.
- **3.2 Anypoint MQ Consumer:** Subscriber-level circuit breaker (`mq.subscriber.circuitBreaker.tripTimeout` / `errorsThreshold`) plus reconnection (`mq.reconnection.frequency` / `attempts`); AUTO ack mode; DLQ for unrecoverable messages.
- **3.3 Salesforce Pub/Sub Event App:** Reconnect on `subscribe-channel-listener`; replay-id-from-object-store enables event-stream resumption on restart; `flow.maxConcurrency` bounds concurrent processing.

